{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Serve an APT package repository from local storage on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A package and repository metadata were created under /srv/local-apt. The enabled service was active, listening on port 8080, and returned valid package metadata over HTTP.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f9c403f123d54eeb","cmd-9ae5f86843b84324"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep the usual remote repositories unreachable while retaining access to the local repository.","status":"satisfied","summary":"APT was configured with an unreachable proxy for ordinary HTTP/HTTPS repositories and a direct exception for node1. The update showed connection failures for every configured remote repository while successfully fetching the local Packages index.","evidence_ids":["cmd-255781c425a3402d","cmd-ff71efc5de154e2e"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Install a package from the local repository while the remote repositories are unreachable.","status":"satisfied","summary":"APT policy selected version 1.0-1 from node1:8080, apt-get fetched it from that origin, dpkg reported it installed, and its executable ran successfully.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ff71efc5de154e2e","cmd-c0246bae74e84aaa"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"All state-changing commands had a clear role in building and serving the repository, enforcing the offline condition, installing the package, or performing the required restart verification. No unnecessary troubleshooting mutations were identified. Package consistency remained healthy and no failed services were observed. One minor abandoned evidence artifact, /tmp/repo-post-packages, remained after the final check; it was created for bounded post-restart HTTP verification but was not cleaned up. The retained local APT source, offline proxy configuration, installed package, repository files, and service were task-related.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f9c403f123d54eeb","cmd-197990cdcbac4d79","cmd-255781c425a3402d","cmd-ff71efc5de154e2e","cmd-c0246bae74e84aaa","cmd-26bb724c84f64e54","cmd-7e559f32d706463c","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are directly demonstrated. The provider-wide restart protocol was also complete: it captured a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged the reboot, observed temporary SSH unavailability, recorded a different boot ID, and verified recovery of the repository service, repository data, APT origin, installed package, and executable. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the reboot.","limitations":["The fixed after-executor listening-sockets snapshot was empty despite the direct post-restart command showing a port-8080 listener and a successful HTTP 200 response; this is a minor collector inconsistency.","The after-executor snapshot shows the bounded verification file /tmp/repo-post-packages remained on node1."]}
